   199	Writers MUST NOT create this legacy form.
   200	
   201	## 5. Project manifests
   202	
   203	`Skillfile.json` conforms to `skillfile-v1.schema.json`. It contains unique
   204	skill declarations and exactly one of `tag`, `branch`, or `revision` for each
   205	skill. `source` is a portable relative path below the manager's configured
   206	source root. `git` is used when the source repository is absent. Branches are
   207	permitted only for direct project declarations and development substitutions.
   208	
   209	`project.alias`, when present, is a non-empty, case-sensitive Unicode label of
   210	at most 128 characters with no control characters. It is an operator-facing
   211	matching label, not a filesystem identifier, and therefore MAY contain spaces.
   212	
   213	Effective agents are selected in this order: manifest `agents`, registered
   214	project agents, manager defaults. Effective locale is manifest `locale`, then
   215	the manager preference.
   216	
   217	`Skillfile.dev.json` conforms to `skillfile-dev-v1.schema.json` and is never
   218	committed. Each substitution is exactly one of a local git checkout `path` or
   219	`git` plus exact `ref`. A substitution replaces every requirement of that name,
   220	skips its normal unification check, is recorded in the marker, and causes
   221	strict audit mode to fail.
   222	
   223	## 6. Sources and snapshots
   224	
   225	### 6.1 Canonical source identity
   226	
   227	Network git sources use a canonical identity. Local paths and `file:` URLs have
   228	no network identity. Protocol 1.0 network URLs:
   229	
   230	- use `ssh`, `git`, `http`, or `https`, or SCP form `[user@]host:path`;
   231	- have an ASCII host matching `[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9.-]*`;
   232	- contain no explicit port, password, query, fragment, percent escape, or
   233	  backslash;
   234	- contain a non-empty portable repository path with no whitespace, `%`, `?`,
   235	  or `#` character;
   236	- produce a canonical `host/path` identity of at most 4096 Unicode scalar
   237	  values.
   238	
   239	Canonicalization lowercases the host, removes user and transport, trims outer
   240	path slashes, and removes one case-sensitive trailing `.git`. Repository path
   241	case is preserved. The result is `host/path`. Invalid network forms MUST be
   242	rejected, not treated as local.
   243	
   244	Allowlist matching is segment-aware: identity `h/a/b` matches prefix `h/a` but
   245	not `h/a-evil`. An empty allowlist permits all network identities. Local
   246	sources bypass the network allowlist.
   247	
   248	### 6.2 Git safety and references
   249	
   250	Git execution MUST restrict protocols to `file`, `git`, `http`, `https`, and
   251	`ssh`; refuse empty or dash-prefixed operands; and place untrusted operands
   252	after `--` where supported. Submodules are unsupported. Archive extraction
