   205	    "secrets": "none",
   206	    "env_read": []
   207	  },
   208	  "dependencies": {}
   209	}
   210	```
   211	
   212	Root-module commands use `"source_dir": "."`; no empty-string alias is permitted.
   213	
   214	### 3.3 Invalid package-controlled arguments
   215	
   216	This object must fail schema validation because `args` is unknown. The same applies to `env`, `flags`, `tags`, `output`, `toolchain`, `build_script`, and `post_build`.
   217	
   218	```json
   219	{
   220	  "type": "build",
   221	  "driver": "go-v1",
   222	  "source_dir": "cmd/golden-tool",
   223	  "args": ["-tags", "package_choice"]
   224	}
   225	```
   226	
   227	### 3.4 Semantic validation rules
   228	
   229	After JSON Schema succeeds, the manager must enforce all of these rules:
   230	
   231	1. A `build` command is legal only in manifest schema 6. Legacy `agents/runtime.json` commands cannot express it.
   232	2. `driver` must equal the closed identifier `go-v1`. Unsupported drivers fail; there is no fallback to a system build command.
   233	3. `source_dir` is either exactly `.` or a portable relative path. After path joining and canonicalization it must be a real directory inside the immutable snapshot. Every component must satisfy the existing no-link/no-special-file snapshot rules.
   234	4. The nearest ancestor `go.mod` must exist and its directory must remain inside the snapshot. `GOWORK=off` means a `go.work` file never expands the source boundary.
   235	5. The selected directory must resolve through fixed `go list` semantics to exactly one buildable package named `main`. Package patterns, multiple packages, and library-only packages fail.
   236	6. A command object cannot combine script, system, and build properties. Unknown fields fail before semantics.
   237	7. The manager derives the output basename from the manifest command key. Unix output is `bin/<command>`; Windows output is `bin/<command>.exe`. The package cannot override it.
   238	8. Build commands participate in the existing activation, dependency-command selection, portable-name collision, and shim collision rules exactly like script commands.
   239	9. Active build command names are processed in Unicode code-point/bytewise lexical order within each provider-first closure node. The same normalized ordering is used in receipts and markers.
   240	10. The raw snapshot content hash—not only `source_dir`—is part of build identity. This intentionally favors safe invalidation over maximum cache hits.
   241	11. A build source may be under a `runtime_root`, but generated output never is: outputs live only in manager-owned staging/cache directories and are never injected into prompt context.
   242	12. A manager that cannot enforce the fixed environment, offline module mode, native target, `CGO_ENABLED=0`, and transaction rules must reject the build command rather than approximate it.
   243	
   244	No package or project field is added for arbitrary build arguments. No build-policy override is added to manager or system configuration in v1.
   245	
   300	  "CGO_ENABLED": "0",
   301	  "GOEXPERIMENT": "",
   302	  "GOROOT": "<resolved-trusted-goroot>",
   303	  "GOOS": "<native-goos>",
   304	  "GOARCH": "<native-goarch>",
   305	  "HOME": "<operation-private>/home",
   306	  "TMPDIR": "<operation-private>/tmp",
   307	  "LC_ALL": "C",
   308	  "LANG": "C"
